{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>To find favor for you.</b> Bring a thing fit to find favor for you before Me — that it should be a favor for you; אפיי״מנט בְּלַעַ״ז. And which is the one fit for favor?" "<b>Unblemished, male, among cattle, among sheep, or among goats.</b> But for a bird burnt offering one does not need perfection and maleness, and it is disqualified only by missing a limb (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French apaisement, 'satisfaction/appeasement'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:44.808517450Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}